# Hardware reference cross-check (mandatory)

This project targets the **Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-7B**. Before adding or
changing any board pin, bus, codec, display, touch, SD, Wi-Fi-C6, audio, I2C, RS485, or
related firmware/docs, **consult the local reference materials first** — do not rely on
memory, prior chat, or guessed pin numbers.

## Local canonical sources (check these first)

Prefer files under `reference/` in this repo. Open / search them when coding hardware:

| Doc | Path | Use for |
|-----|------|---------|
| **Board hardware manual / schematic** | `reference/ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-7B.pdf` | Board pinout, connectors, on-board peripherals, schematic nets |
| **ESP32-P4 technical reference manual** | `reference/esp32-p4_technical_reference_manual_en.pdf` | SoC peripherals, registers, bus behaviour |
| **ESP32-P4 datasheet** | `reference/esp32-p4_datasheet_en.pdf` | Electrical limits, package/pin capabilities |
| **Digested pin map (project)** | `reference/hardware_pins.md` | Confirmed GPIO/I2C/audio/SD assignments used by this firmware |
| **Modbus RTU Relay 4CH manual** | `reference/waveshare-modbus-rtu-relay-4ch-manual.pdf` (+ supplement / register-map.md) | Relay board protocol |
| **PT100 RS485 converter** | `reference/BRT-PT100AD-PT100-to-RS485-AD-Converter.pdf` | RTD Modbus board |

**Always start with the board PDF + `hardware_pins.md` for GPIO/connector work.** Use the
Espressif TRM/datasheet when the question is chip capability, not board wiring. Use the
relay/RTD PDFs for Modbus address/register coding.

## Live Waveshare sources (re-check when local notes may be stale)

After local PDFs, verify against current Waveshare pages — especially if `hardware_pins.md`
and the PDF disagree, or before changing pins:

1. **ESP-IDF tutorial + demos (primary online):**
   https://docs.waveshare.com/ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-X/Development-Environment-Setup-IDF
2. **Board wiki / pin overview:**
   https://www.waveshare.com/wiki/ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-7B
3. **Docs hub (same family):**
   https://docs.waveshare.com/ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-7B

When a demo is named (`i2scodec`, `i2c_tools`, `sdmmc`, MIPI-DSI, RS485, etc.), open that
section and, if Waveshare links a sample project, **inspect the sample pin macros**
(MCU `DO`/`DI` / `DOUT`/`DIN`) — not only the prose table.

## How to interpret pin names

Waveshare tables often name signals **from the peripheral's point of view**. ESPHome /
ESP-IDF usually name them **from the ESP's point of view**. Those invert for bidirectional
buses.

**Known trap (a GPIO number is not proof the pin is usable):** `hardware_pins.md` once listed
GPIO20 as an available header net, and firmware ran the door reed on it for weeks. The
schematic shows GPIO20 is the battery-sense divider (`BAT → R92 → GPIO20 → R93 → GND`) and is
not routed to either expansion header. Before assigning a field-I/O pin, confirm on the
schematic that (a) it appears on connector **P1** or **P3**, and (b) it has no other net
attached. Also skip **GPIO34–GPIO38** — ESP32-P4 strapping pins (GPIO34 and GPIO36 are on P3
pins 1–2). The confirmed per-pin P1/P3 map is in `reference/hardware_pins.md`.

**Known trap (audio I2S / ES8311):** Waveshare `ASDOUT` = codec → bus = ESP **input**
(`i2s_din`). Waveshare `DSDIN` = codec ← bus = ESP **output** (`i2s_dout`). Wiring
playback to GPIO11 yields healthy clocks, PA clicks, media player `PLAYING`, and **no
speech**. Official IDF-style mapping for this board family is `I2S_DO=GPIO9`,
`I2S_DI=GPIO11`, `PA_Ctrl=GPIO53`.

## Required workflow

1. **Before** editing substitutions / GPIO / `p4_audio.yaml` / I2C / display / SD / C6
   pins: read the relevant section of `reference/ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-7B.pdf` and
   `reference/hardware_pins.md`. Use TRM/datasheet PDFs when the change depends on SoC
   behaviour. For RS485 relay/RTD work, use those PDFs too.
2. Prefer **schematic / sample code pin `#define`s** over marketing/table wording when
   they disagree.
3. If local PDF and live Waveshare demo disagree, note both, prefer sample/`#define`
   direction, and update `reference/hardware_pins.md` with the citation.
4. After changing pins, update `reference/hardware_pins.md` with the source cited
   (PDF page/section and/or Waveshare URL) and any MCU-vs-peripheral naming note.
5. Do not treat chat memory or unverified web summaries as authoritative over the local
   schematic/manual PDFs.
